    {
      "column_index": 6,
      "header_id": "C112",
      "x_range": [
        4736.4,
        8209.3
      ],
      "section_title": "Practical Example",
      "section_number": null,
      "teaching_text": "Practical Example:\r\n\r\n1- Grid of squarish cells.\r\n\r\n2- Use the \"Boundary\" component to make surfaces out of the cells.\r\n\r\n3- Get the center point of each cell using the \"Area\" component.\r\n\r\n4- Extract the XYZ information from the center points.\r\n\r\n5- Select only the ones with the Y = 15.\r\n\r\n7- Jitter the resultant List.\r\n\r\n6- Organize (sort) these ones from smallest to largest X value.\r\n\r\n7- Back to step 2, randomly cull 25 surfaces.\r\n\r\n8- Back to step 2, use a pattern to cull surfaces.\r\n\r\n9- Back to step 2, find the length of the List of surfaces and split the List in half parametrically.",
      "teaching_panel_id": "C280",
      "additional_teaching_panels": [],
      "sub_annotations": [
        {
